course: dictionary
lesson: 12415
title: The Way of Daoism
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Daoism is a Chinese tradition of thought and religion. Its name comes from the word «Dao», which means «the Way»: the natural flow of the universe. Daoists try to live simply, calmly and in harmony with nature.
explain: Daoism can also mean the religion that grew from these ideas. That religion has temples, priests, festivals and many gods and immortals. The sentence tells you which meaning is used.
explain: «Mei read a book about Daoism.» Here Daoism is a tradition of ideas, because you read about it. «She visited a Daoist temple in China.» Here the word Daoist describes the temple, so Daoism is the religion.
fact: Daoism is also spelled Taoism.
fact: «Dao» means «the Way», the natural flow of the universe.
fact: Laozi is the teacher linked to Daoism, and «Dao De Jing» is its famous book.
fact: The yin-yang symbol shows how opposites, like dark and light, balance each other.
fact: Daoism focuses on nature and going with the flow, while Confucianism focuses more on rules and duties.
exercise: «Mei learned about Daoism in her lesson on China.» What is Daoism? | A sport played on ice | A type of Chinese noodle | *A Chinese tradition of thought based on «the Way»
exercise: What does the word «Dao» mean? | *The Way, the natural flow of the universe | A kind of Chinese tea | A large stone temple
exercise: Which symbol shows how opposites, like dark and light, balance each other? | A red lantern | *Yin-yang | A dragon
test: Taoism is another spelling of which word? | Tai chi | Dragon | *Daoism
test: Daoism focuses on nature and going with the flow, while Confucianism focuses on what? | Music and dance | *Rules and duties | Sport and games
exam: What does the Daoist way of life aim for? | *Living simply and in harmony with nature | Winning every contest | Owning as many things as possible
